      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Los hermanos de Māui eran los mejores pescadores. Navegaban más allá del arrecife, al mar profundo.",
          "en": "Māui’s brothers were the best fishermen. They sailed past the reef to the deep sea."
        },
        {
          "es": "Māui no era gran pescador. Pero era astuto y le encantaban los trucos.",
          "en": "Māui was not a great fisherman. But he was clever, and he loved tricks."
        },
        {
          "es": "Cuando un hermano sacaba un pez grande, Māui gritaba: «¡Cuidado! ¡Tu cuerda está floja!»",
          "en": "When a brother pulled in a big fish, Māui shouted, “Careful! Your line is loose!”"
        },
        {
          "es": "En la confusión, lanzaba el pez a su propia canoa. Y lo mostraba como si fuera suyo.",
          "en": "In the confusion, he flipped the fish into his own canoe. Then he showed it off as his catch."
        },
        {
          "es": "Pronto los hermanos se negaron a llevarlo a pescar. Hina también lo regañó.",
          "en": "Soon the brothers refused to take him fishing. Hina scolded him too."
        },
        {
          "es": "Māui se quedó callado. Estaba planeando algo más grande que cualquier truco.",
          "en": "Māui went quiet. He was planning something bigger than any trick."
        }
      ],
