      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "En un canto antiguo, Hina manda a Māui a pedirle un anzuelo a su padre.",
          "en": "In an old chant, Hina sends Māui to his father to ask for a hook."
        },
        {
          "es": "El anzuelo se llamaba Manaiakalani. El nombre significa «amarrado al cielo».",
          "en": "The hook was called Manaiakalani. The name means “made fast to the heavens.”"
        },
        {
          "es": "Era de hueso sagrado, atado con una cuerda de lianas trenzadas.",
          "en": "It was made of sacred bone, tied with a cord of twisted vines."
        },
        {
          "es": "Su línea era de olonā, una fibra tan fuerte que podía sacar peces enormes.",
          "en": "Its line was made of olonā, a plant fiber so strong it could haul up huge fish."
        },
        {
          "es": "De carnada, Māui eligió al ʻalae, un ave negra de agua, sagrada para Hina.",
          "en": "For bait, Māui chose the ʻalae, a black water bird that was sacred to Hina."
        }
      ],
